1
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:15,724
AS YOU STOOD BY

2
00:00:16,975 --> 00:00:20,270
EUN-SU, HUI-SU AND JIN-PYO

3
00:00:29,279 --> 00:00:30,320
Get ready.

4
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:33,283
Sure, do your worst.

5
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:38,705
Yes, I'm heading back right now.

6
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:25,417
Don't you dare!

7
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:27,337
No! No!

8
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:32,174
Why should he get to control your life?

9
00:01:32,175 --> 00:01:34,135
If you don't leave him, you'll die.

10
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:38,264
The only thing that will end this
is if someone dies.

11
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:41,851
<i>You're not gonna die.</i>

12
00:01:44,395 --> 00:01:46,147
If anyone's gonna die, it's Jin-pyo.

13
00:01:51,736 --> 00:01:54,655
No! He can't see you! Eun-su! No!

14
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:07,334
Ah shit.

15
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:39,826
What a mess.

16
00:02:58,136 --> 00:02:59,428
I shouldn't have done it.

17
00:02:59,429 --> 00:03:02,097
Mistakes have consequences.

18
00:03:02,098 --> 00:03:03,600
Wait!

19
00:03:07,604 --> 00:03:08,937
Put that back on.

20
00:03:08,938 --> 00:03:10,522
I won't embarrass you again--

21
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:26,497
Jin-pyo!

22
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:28,916
Wait!

23
00:03:33,171 --> 00:03:36,257
I'll visit Mrs. Kim tomorrow
and beg for forgiveness.

24
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:40,677
I'll say it was my medication!

25
00:03:40,678 --> 00:03:43,847
No one will know what goes on between us.
I'll fix everything.

26
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:47,936
Do you really think
that's anyone's concern?

27
00:03:49,103 --> 00:03:50,812
Please don't!

28
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:52,064
I said I'll fix it!

29
00:04:06,412 --> 00:04:07,538
Stay right there.

30
00:04:11,459 --> 00:04:13,001
Don't come out, no matter what.

31
00:04:13,002 --> 00:04:14,629
I can't just let him hurt you.

32
00:04:19,509 --> 00:04:21,052
You said to do my worst?

33
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:23,429
Careful what you wish for.

34
00:04:24,931 --> 00:04:27,557
You insulted a client
whose account could change my career,

35
00:04:27,558 --> 00:04:29,851
so you'd better hope
the US market goes up tonight.

36
00:04:29,852 --> 00:04:31,770
Since the markets usually go my way

37
00:04:31,771 --> 00:04:35,440
the day after I teach you a lesson.

38
00:04:48,496 --> 00:04:50,080
Sh!

39
00:04:50,081 --> 00:04:51,331
Yes, sir?

40
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:53,293
No, I haven't been able to reach her.

41
00:04:53,876 --> 00:04:55,294
I assume she has her phone off.

42
00:04:56,629 --> 00:04:57,714
Right.

43
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:00,008
I already left her two.

44
00:05:00,925 --> 00:05:02,468
It is rather late, sir.

45
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:04,721
Of course, sir.

46
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:09,349
I said shut it!
You have me apologizing to that idiot,

47
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:11,727
instead of celebrating
what should've been a win!

48
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:13,896
If Mrs. Kim decides to drop us,

49
00:05:15,398 --> 00:05:16,482
my worst,

50
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:18,776
that you asked for,

51
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:21,903
will be worse than ever.

52
00:05:43,009 --> 00:05:44,052
Hui-su.

53
00:05:47,305 --> 00:05:48,890
You can't...

54
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:13,873
DEARLY DEPARTED
MS. KANG HUI-YEON

55
00:06:34,769 --> 00:06:36,521
<i>I'm sorry, Mrs. Kang.</i>

56
00:06:38,523 --> 00:06:39,857
<i>Please help me.</i>

57
00:07:55,766 --> 00:07:57,684
Hui-su!

58
00:08:12,825 --> 00:08:13,743
Hey!

59
00:08:15,077 --> 00:08:17,746
Talk to me. Hui-su! Please!

60
00:08:19,874 --> 00:08:20,958
I need to...

61
00:08:33,221 --> 00:08:35,598
AMBULANCE

62
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:05,711
That's enough.

63
00:09:07,505 --> 00:09:09,715
You need to... You need to wake up.

64
00:09:10,299 --> 00:09:11,133
Come on!

65
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:30,318
Hey, you don't kill yourself.

66
00:09:30,319 --> 00:09:32,153
You don't get to decide. You don't!

67
00:09:32,154 --> 00:09:33,947
If you don't want me to do it...

68
00:09:35,616 --> 00:09:37,577
...then get rid of that thing.

69
00:09:40,162 --> 00:09:43,207
I'll put up with the beatings
when you lose control.

70
00:09:44,875 --> 00:09:49,088
I am not gonna put up with
you treating me like a monkey in a zoo.

71
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:51,673
Get rid of it.

72
00:09:56,762 --> 00:09:58,389
That is never gonna happen.

73
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:06,731
Stop!

74
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:09,983
No!

75
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:11,610
Drop it!

76
00:11:20,513 --> 00:11:21,722
<i>I'll do it.</i>

77
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:24,016
<i>I have to.</i>

78
00:11:38,989 --> 00:11:40,741
<i>It won't be easy.</i>

79
00:11:42,201 --> 00:11:44,495
<i>And even when it's done,</i>

80
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:46,288
<i>it won't be over.</i>

81
00:11:47,748 --> 00:11:49,375
<i>But if we just...</i>

82
00:11:55,923 --> 00:12:01,303
EUN-SU

83
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:32,752
<i>I'm in.</i>

84
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:35,087
<i>We can do this.</i>

85
00:13:21,258 --> 00:13:23,760
<i>Dear residents,
this is an important message</i>

86
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:26,054
<i>from building management.</i>

87
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:30,225
<i>We would like to remind you that smoking
is prohibited in all indoor areas</i>

88
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:31,601
<i>and on private balconies.</i>

89
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:34,187
<i>We have received
numerous complaints about smoke</i>

90
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:36,898
<i>traveling through vents and windows.</i>

91
00:13:36,899 --> 00:13:41,069
<i>Residents on higher floors
have been particularly inconvenienced,</i>

92
00:13:41,070 --> 00:13:43,822
<i>and we ask that everyone respect
the nonsmoking rule.</i>

93
00:13:43,823 --> 00:13:47,534
<i>Should we keep receiving complaints
about specific units,</i>

94
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:50,995
<i>we will need to meet with the residents
to resolve the matter.</i>

95
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:53,665
<i>Once again, building management
reminds you that smoking</i>

96
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:55,292
<i>is prohibited in all areas...</i>

97
00:14:30,744 --> 00:14:33,746
<i>...and we ask that everyone respect
the nonsmoking rules.</i>

98
00:14:33,747 --> 00:14:34,831
I'm going!

99
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:37,083
<i>If we keep receiving complaints
about specific units,</i>

100
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:39,711
<i>we will need to meet
with the residents to resolve the matter.</i>

101
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:43,883
<i>Once again, building management
reminds you that smoking is prohibited...</i>

102
00:15:14,121 --> 00:15:15,205
Screwdriver?

103
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:20,668
Yes. It's only about three inches.

104
00:15:20,669 --> 00:15:23,881
I think I forgot to put it away
after I changed your strap.

105
00:15:53,702 --> 00:15:55,578
Nope, I don't see it.

106
00:15:55,579 --> 00:15:59,458
Uh, thanks, I guess I used it
to fix another watch after and forgot.

107
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:17,309
Is the new strap comfortable
and fitting right?

108
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,604
It's fine.

109
00:16:22,856 --> 00:16:23,899
Oh, good.

110
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,905
What you said when I was here last,

111
00:16:30,781 --> 00:16:32,658
I don't think it makes sense.

112
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:34,284
Which part?

113
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:38,789
She should've killed her husband.
Why did she die such an unfair death?

114
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:44,044
Yeah, so?

115
00:16:46,422 --> 00:16:48,924
It's not worth killing him
if you end up in prison.

116
00:16:56,974 --> 00:16:58,892
All the more reason not to get caught.

117
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:04,480
How do you kill someone
and not get caught?

118
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:06,817
Make sure no one knows you did it,

119
00:17:07,443 --> 00:17:09,653
or make sure no one knows he's dead.

120
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:12,572
You watch way too many movies.

121
00:17:12,573 --> 00:17:15,366
What can they do
if there's no body to prove it?

122
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,006
Why you asking?

123
00:17:34,636 --> 00:17:38,347
Ah. You went to the funeral
and saw the husband there, didn't you?

124
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:39,558
Please don't!

125
00:17:42,394 --> 00:17:43,353
Yeah.

126
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:49,401
Now I'm not gonna get any work done.

127
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,281
You're coming.

128
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:57,742
We'll go have the <i>haejang-guk</i> you owe me.

129
00:17:57,743 --> 00:17:59,578
I have to get back to work.

130
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,121
I'm already late.

131
00:18:11,381 --> 00:18:12,800
Hello, miss!

132
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:20,516
JINGANG CHINESE MARKET

133
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,032
- Mr. Jin, is there--
- Not right now.

134
00:18:39,743 --> 00:18:40,911
Jang Kang.

135
00:18:42,746 --> 00:18:44,498
Take that out first.

136
00:18:45,749 --> 00:18:48,001
You're gonna need to do it in two trips.

137
00:18:51,922 --> 00:18:53,590
I can make it all in one, sir.

138
00:18:54,383 --> 00:18:57,343
I don't want you getting hurt
and stuck with a huge medical bill.

139
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:59,179
Do it in two, please.

140
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:00,889
Oh.

141
00:19:02,432 --> 00:19:04,434
I didn't think of that. Thank you.

142
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:12,151
Did you need something?

143
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:15,821
I can go and have the soup
with you after all.

144
00:19:38,468 --> 00:19:40,929
You didn't know
what I was gonna pull out, did ya?

145
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:54,942
Whoa, hey, hey!

146
00:19:54,943 --> 00:19:56,820
- Um, my apologies, sir.
- Idiot!

147
00:19:58,864 --> 00:20:00,448
He's pretty nervous.

148
00:20:00,449 --> 00:20:01,658
Is he illegal?

149
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:05,537
Pretty much.

150
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:08,415
Where'd he come from?

151
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:10,500
Stowed away.

152
00:20:13,003 --> 00:20:14,296
Without a passport?

153
00:20:14,963 --> 00:20:17,715
Either he couldn't afford one,
or he had to run.

154
00:20:17,716 --> 00:20:19,676
Probably no papers.

155
00:20:26,516 --> 00:20:29,102
<i>What can they do
if there's no body to prove it?</i>

156
00:20:58,382 --> 00:21:01,969
You're sure Jin-pyo doesn't have
any relatives in China? At all?

157
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:04,304
Positive.

158
00:21:11,103 --> 00:21:12,437
This could work.

159
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:37,296
Excuse me, sir.

160
00:21:42,634 --> 00:21:44,344
May I have a minute of your time?

161
00:21:47,806 --> 00:21:49,391
That's a lot of money.

162
00:21:51,268 --> 00:21:52,644
And all I'd do

163
00:21:53,562 --> 00:21:55,813
is use a guy's passport

164
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:58,399
and fly to Shanghai?

165
00:22:00,485 --> 00:22:01,736
It is quite a lot of money,

166
00:22:01,737 --> 00:22:04,781
and the only condition
is that you don't ask any questions.

167
00:22:08,785 --> 00:22:09,785
Just do as I say,

168
00:22:09,786 --> 00:22:12,372
and you won't have any trouble
getting back to China.

169
00:22:14,041 --> 00:22:17,502
I suppose you had to learn to keep quiet,
considering how you made your way here.

170
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:27,386
You can say no and keep scraping by,
hiding every time you see a cop car,

171
00:22:27,387 --> 00:22:31,224
or go back home to your family
with a nice wad of cash in your pocket.

172
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:33,310
Think it over, Mr. Jang.

173
00:22:35,103 --> 00:22:38,482
You'll be heading home in first class,
not smuggled in the hold of a ship.

174
00:22:43,653 --> 00:22:45,614
Call me in three days with your answer.

175
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:49,785
You need it that soon?

176
00:22:50,702 --> 00:22:51,536
Yeah.

177
00:23:00,712 --> 00:23:02,047
Just one question.

178
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:06,051
It would really help me make a decision.

179
00:23:15,394 --> 00:23:16,937
Is this person...

180
00:23:20,399 --> 00:23:21,733
Is he alive?

181
00:23:33,954 --> 00:23:35,997
He's alive. What are you talking about?

182
00:23:41,420 --> 00:23:43,296
It's okay. He didn't notice.

183
00:23:47,717 --> 00:23:50,553
I was freaked out
the second you guys walked in.

184
00:23:50,554 --> 00:23:52,388
He looks so much like him.

185
00:23:52,389 --> 00:23:55,433
I know. Luckily, he doesn't have
that same poker face.

186
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:58,520
From what I saw, he won't even
take the three days to answer.

187
00:23:59,855 --> 00:24:01,982
But he seems like a decent guy, at least.

188
00:24:04,151 --> 00:24:07,821
If we do this thing right,
Jin-pyo will go missing in China.

189
00:24:08,655 --> 00:24:11,866
All we're missing is a reason for him
to get on a plane and head over there.

190
00:24:28,925 --> 00:24:31,802
<i>The person
you are trying to reach is unavailable.</i>

191
00:24:31,803 --> 00:24:33,721
<i>Please leave a message after the tone.</i>

192
00:24:36,766 --> 00:24:38,185
MS. KIM MI-GYEONG

193
00:24:44,524 --> 00:24:45,442
Hey.

194
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:47,694
How'd it go?

195
00:24:49,571 --> 00:24:51,072
I'd say it went very well.

196
00:24:51,948 --> 00:24:53,575
We should have her back here soon.

197
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:57,036
Great.

198
00:25:03,835 --> 00:25:06,254
I wholeheartedly agree
with you, Mrs. Kim.

199
00:25:07,172 --> 00:25:10,841
He's smart and hardworking,
and an excellent strategist.

200
00:25:10,842 --> 00:25:14,011
Normally, I would stand by him 100%,

201
00:25:14,012 --> 00:25:16,222
but the disrespect
he showed you that evening,

202
00:25:16,223 --> 00:25:18,850
and on such an important occasion for you.

203
00:25:19,392 --> 00:25:21,685
Please accept my deepest apologies.

204
00:25:21,686 --> 00:25:25,105
I do hope you can see beyond
Mr. Noh's transgression and forgive us.

205
00:25:25,106 --> 00:25:29,026
I would be honored if you allowed me to
put together a team of talented advisers.

206
00:25:29,027 --> 00:25:32,738
They'll treat you and your valuable assets
with the respect they deserve.

207
00:25:32,739 --> 00:25:34,449
I'll see to it myself.

208
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:37,577
Thank you, Mrs. Kim.
We won't let you down.

209
00:25:38,119 --> 00:25:39,496
Yes, you too.

210
00:25:39,996 --> 00:25:41,956
Uh, yes, that's our motto.

211
00:25:41,957 --> 00:25:42,873
Bye, now.

212
00:25:45,877 --> 00:25:48,088
CLIENT PROFILE
KIM MI-GYEONG

213
00:26:05,855 --> 00:26:07,566
Lavie Department Store?

214
00:26:34,968 --> 00:26:37,220
DOWNLOAD COMPLETE

215
00:27:24,142 --> 00:27:26,102
I thought we could go out
for a nice dinner.

216
00:27:27,979 --> 00:27:29,648
You can even choose your own outfit.

217
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:32,859
I'll wait for you here.

218
00:27:57,342 --> 00:27:58,885
You made a good choice.

219
00:28:00,178 --> 00:28:02,597
Pretty, and it covers up
all the right places.

220
00:28:15,860 --> 00:28:17,362
Good to see you, Eun-su.

221
00:28:17,987 --> 00:28:19,029
Good to see you too.

222
00:28:19,030 --> 00:28:20,240
Oh, thank you.

223
00:28:22,701 --> 00:28:23,827
Hui-su.

224
00:28:24,411 --> 00:28:25,286
Hi, Eun-su.

225
00:28:27,038 --> 00:28:30,582
You haven't seen each other in a while,
so I thought I'd surprise you both.

226
00:28:30,583 --> 00:28:32,001
I think it worked.

227
00:28:32,836 --> 00:28:33,670
Sure did.

228
00:28:34,337 --> 00:28:35,921
You're glad, aren't you?

229
00:28:35,922 --> 00:28:38,216
Yes, thanks.

230
00:28:39,426 --> 00:28:40,468
Over here.

231
00:28:53,898 --> 00:28:56,233
Here's to seeing you away from work, hmm?

232
00:28:56,234 --> 00:28:58,319
Right.

233
00:28:59,070 --> 00:29:00,405
And...

234
00:29:00,989 --> 00:29:02,322
...here's to the girl we love.

235
00:29:02,323 --> 00:29:04,159
Oh no! I'm so sorry.

236
00:29:04,784 --> 00:29:05,618
Oh.

237
00:29:06,119 --> 00:29:08,204
Your jacket. It's all soaked.

238
00:29:08,705 --> 00:29:10,372
I got you everywhere.

239
00:29:10,373 --> 00:29:11,791
Excuse me?

240
00:29:13,334 --> 00:29:15,627
I'm sorry. What a mess.

241
00:29:15,628 --> 00:29:17,337
It's fine. It's not that bad.

242
00:29:17,338 --> 00:29:19,465
- You called, sir?
- Yes, I spilled a glass of wine.

243
00:29:19,466 --> 00:29:21,300
I can help you with that, ma'am.

244
00:29:21,301 --> 00:29:22,301
It's fine.

245
00:29:22,302 --> 00:29:24,721
You should go with her.
We'll wait for you to order.

246
00:29:26,222 --> 00:29:28,099
Okay, I'll try to make it quick.

247
00:29:39,068 --> 00:29:39,903
What's new?

248
00:29:41,488 --> 00:29:43,280
You know, I should check on Hui-su.

249
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:44,449
The closet.

250
00:29:47,702 --> 00:29:49,120
You were there that night.

251
00:29:57,337 --> 00:30:00,006
I think what you heard
might have given you the wrong idea.

252
00:30:01,674 --> 00:30:02,717
Hui-su

253
00:30:04,260 --> 00:30:05,261
is pretty sick.

254
00:30:20,527 --> 00:30:21,820
She struggles.

255
00:30:23,488 --> 00:30:25,698
Her mother's situation hit her hard.

256
00:30:28,284 --> 00:30:31,538
<i>And after the miscarriage,
she gave up writing altogether.</i>

257
00:30:32,038 --> 00:30:34,874
Ever since, she's been anxious
and having dark thoughts.

258
00:30:36,042 --> 00:30:39,379
I had to install a monitor
to make sure she's okay when I'm gone.

259
00:30:40,713 --> 00:30:43,132
She thinks I wanted to spy on her.

260
00:30:47,345 --> 00:30:48,471
<i>I'm worried.</i>

261
00:30:51,266 --> 00:30:52,851
I think she's having a breakdown.

262
00:30:55,019 --> 00:30:56,896
The beatings can't be helping that.

263
00:31:08,116 --> 00:31:10,868
Some things need to stay
between husband and wife.

264
00:31:10,869 --> 00:31:12,412
Violence is private, huh?

265
00:31:24,424 --> 00:31:27,010
If you had love in your life,
you would understand.

266
00:31:28,136 --> 00:31:30,722
Hui-su would die if we weren't together.

267
00:31:32,056 --> 00:31:33,725
And I'd be lost without her too.

268
00:31:35,643 --> 00:31:37,019
That's what marriage is.

269
00:31:37,020 --> 00:31:39,480
So having love means
having to get beaten, is that it?

270
00:31:42,942 --> 00:31:44,444
I'd watch it if I were you.

271
00:31:49,991 --> 00:31:52,368
'Cause when I get challenged,
your friend gets hurt.

272
00:31:58,291 --> 00:32:00,834
You'll be taking it out on her
again tonight, won't you?

273
00:32:12,847 --> 00:32:16,225
Did I tell you I found a way
to smooth things over with Mrs. Kim?

274
00:32:17,226 --> 00:32:19,020
I don't have to go see her?

275
00:32:20,521 --> 00:32:23,149
Turns out,
she and Eun-su have a connection.

276
00:32:39,540 --> 00:32:41,917
<i>I'm always amazed
at what a small world this is.</i>

277
00:32:41,918 --> 00:32:43,502
<i>Such a happy coincidence.</i>

278
00:32:43,503 --> 00:32:46,047
Hui-su has been quite troubled by this,

279
00:32:46,547 --> 00:32:48,508
so I take it you will step in to help?

280
00:32:56,349 --> 00:32:58,225
{\an8}MS. KIM MI-GYEONG
CHEONGDAM-DONG

281
00:32:58,226 --> 00:33:02,521
{\an8}HOPES TO HOLD SOLO EXHIBITION
BEFORE TURNING 60

282
00:33:02,522 --> 00:33:05,190
{\an8}I've always wanted
to see your first piece.

283
00:33:05,191 --> 00:33:08,235
It's such an honor to see it here
in your studio, Mrs. Kim.

284
00:33:08,236 --> 00:33:11,321
Compared to what you did for me back then,
this is nothing.

285
00:33:11,322 --> 00:33:14,408
I don't know if I did much,
seeing as I had just started that job.

286
00:33:14,409 --> 00:33:17,077
I only ran as fast as I could
to impress my boss.

287
00:33:17,078 --> 00:33:20,664
You got there ahead of both the tow truck
and the police. You saved me.

288
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:23,333
My mother-in-law
betrayed me viciously that day.

289
00:33:23,334 --> 00:33:24,334
If it weren't for you,

290
00:33:24,335 --> 00:33:27,713
I would've been left freezing in
the middle of that terrible neighborhood.

291
00:33:27,714 --> 00:33:29,465
Utterly depressed and wanting to die.

292
00:33:30,967 --> 00:33:32,552
Would you like a cup of tea?

293
00:33:34,178 --> 00:33:35,179
Mrs. Kim.

294
00:33:36,431 --> 00:33:40,059
You said if I ever need a favor?

295
00:33:51,612 --> 00:33:53,239
Pardon me, where's the restroom?

296
00:33:57,118 --> 00:33:58,036
Thank you

297
00:33:59,287 --> 00:34:00,454
for agreeing to see me again.

298
00:34:00,455 --> 00:34:02,749
You should
save your gratitude for Ms. Jo.

299
00:34:04,083 --> 00:34:06,418
I will accept your apology
and consider the matter closed,

300
00:34:06,419 --> 00:34:08,296
so this conversation's over.

301
00:34:08,796 --> 00:34:10,006
And please stop calling.

302
00:34:15,511 --> 00:34:19,347
That's what you decided to do
with the one favor I owed you?

303
00:34:19,348 --> 00:34:21,184
I expected something bigger.

304
00:34:25,563 --> 00:34:27,773
It's always been a dream of yours,
hasn't it?

305
00:34:27,774 --> 00:34:30,567
Putting on a solo exhibit
before you turn 60?

306
00:34:30,568 --> 00:34:32,277
You remember that?

307
00:34:32,278 --> 00:34:34,529
I wish my mom
could have a life like yours,

308
00:34:34,530 --> 00:34:38,159
full of dreams and big ideas.

309
00:34:41,204 --> 00:34:45,207
I thought how nice it must be when you can
spend your days pursuing your passion.

310
00:35:15,196 --> 00:35:16,571
I'll take over from here.

311
00:35:16,572 --> 00:35:19,075
Sorry, Mrs. Kim.
I didn't know you were coming today.

312
00:35:27,125 --> 00:35:28,126
Huh.

313
00:35:30,044 --> 00:35:33,296
You will ensure that none of this
gets back to my husband.

314
00:35:33,297 --> 00:35:36,759
And I... want nothing linked directly to me.

315
00:35:37,468 --> 00:35:40,303
Yes. We'll use utmost discretion.

316
00:35:40,304 --> 00:35:43,474
Our most important clients
do prefer a quieter approach.

317
00:35:44,100 --> 00:35:46,060
Rest assured, we'll protect your privacy.

318
00:35:57,613 --> 00:36:00,992
<i>If you do not cross the line,
Hui-su will not get hurt.</i>

319
00:36:01,951 --> 00:36:04,912
<i>Marital affairs are best
left between husband and wife.</i>

320
00:36:17,925 --> 00:36:20,052
I know it hasn't been a month already.

321
00:36:21,012 --> 00:36:23,848
You're not open today,
so it doesn't count as gym time.

322
00:36:28,477 --> 00:36:30,478
Go. Come back in a month.

323
00:36:30,479 --> 00:36:32,231
Or not at all, for all I care.

324
00:36:32,732 --> 00:36:34,108
I need this place.

325
00:36:36,736 --> 00:36:39,322
You won't even know I'm there. I swear.

326
00:37:45,972 --> 00:37:50,685
{\an8}SOGANG UNIVERSITY, ECHO, JO EUN-SU

327
00:38:10,288 --> 00:38:12,247
MR. JANG KANG

328
00:38:13,791 --> 00:38:14,834
Hello?

329
00:38:15,793 --> 00:38:16,711
<i>Hi.</i>

330
00:38:19,005 --> 00:38:20,423
<i>The passport thing?</i>

331
00:38:21,257 --> 00:38:22,216
<i>I'll do it.</i>

332
00:38:25,761 --> 00:38:27,805
You're willing to go back to China?

333
00:38:28,889 --> 00:38:29,849
<i>Yes.</i>

334
00:38:31,684 --> 00:38:33,059
<i>I miss my son.</i>

335
00:38:58,794 --> 00:38:59,837
Thank you.

336
00:39:21,192 --> 00:39:22,359
I finished my run, sir.

337
00:39:22,360 --> 00:39:24,195
Did I see you getting out of a car?

338
00:39:27,865 --> 00:39:28,783
Yeah.

339
00:39:29,533 --> 00:39:31,327
A friend from home is in town.

340
00:39:33,204 --> 00:39:34,330
Hey!

341
00:39:35,122 --> 00:39:37,208
A friend from back home, huh?

342
00:39:39,877 --> 00:39:41,212
Must have been nice.

343
00:39:42,004 --> 00:39:43,255
- Yeah.
- Good.

344
00:39:44,507 --> 00:39:45,507
You can go.

345
00:40:12,243 --> 00:40:14,411
Using Mrs. Kim's account?

346
00:40:14,412 --> 00:40:18,165
Since your husband requested the meeting,
it's the best way to avoid suspicion.

347
00:40:18,749 --> 00:40:19,875
Oh.

348
00:40:20,668 --> 00:40:23,546
I feel bad knowing
that she'll lose money on this.

349
00:40:24,547 --> 00:40:27,841
We didn't have a choice.
Although, the firm will help her.

350
00:40:27,842 --> 00:40:29,843
They'll be able to cover it,
and more importantly,

351
00:40:29,844 --> 00:40:31,470
make sure it stays quiet.

352
00:40:32,012 --> 00:40:33,347
She's a strong woman.

353
00:40:34,223 --> 00:40:35,724
She's gotten over worse.

354
00:40:38,519 --> 00:40:39,979
I see Jang. We'll talk later.

355
00:40:41,063 --> 00:40:42,189
Oh.

356
00:40:59,039 --> 00:41:02,333
I was so surprised when I looked
in the mirror. I barely recognized myself.

357
00:41:02,334 --> 00:41:03,711
I guess, uh,

358
00:41:04,420 --> 00:41:05,754
I'll get used to it.

359
00:41:06,380 --> 00:41:08,007
You do look really good.

360
00:41:08,549 --> 00:41:09,632
- Oh, let me.
- Ah.

361
00:41:09,633 --> 00:41:11,051
I can take that.

362
00:41:11,844 --> 00:41:13,262
Wow, all this?

363
00:41:14,513 --> 00:41:17,558
Uh, tilt your head a little. Bend down.

364
00:41:19,518 --> 00:41:22,395
Oh. There was something in my hair, huh?

365
00:41:22,396 --> 00:41:24,148
Uh... Oh, here too.

366
00:41:32,198 --> 00:41:33,032
Pull over.

367
00:41:45,544 --> 00:41:47,338
Captain! We're gonna be late!

368
00:41:51,759 --> 00:41:53,843
It'll help if you use the siren.

369
00:41:53,844 --> 00:41:54,928
Right.

370
00:42:02,937 --> 00:42:04,146
Is everything all right?

371
00:42:05,022 --> 00:42:06,106
No, we're good.

372
00:42:08,984 --> 00:42:10,235
<i>Jin-pyo,</i>

373
00:42:10,236 --> 00:42:13,071
<i>the Presidential Office evaluation
is coming up soon.</i>

374
00:42:13,072 --> 00:42:14,031
CHOI WON-HO

375
00:42:21,664 --> 00:42:23,165
We should be there in five.

376
00:42:23,666 --> 00:42:26,084
I'll let you know what's happening
when we get there.

377
00:42:41,308 --> 00:42:42,350
{\an8}MINE

378
00:42:42,351 --> 00:42:44,812
{\an8}BREEZEHILL, 42-78
APGUJEONG-RO, GANGNAM-GU, SEOUL

379
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:57,532
Looks like I'll get promoted
before my sister even gets evaluated.

380
00:42:59,285 --> 00:43:00,661
Have you gotten

381
00:43:01,829 --> 00:43:02,871
even more beautiful?

382
00:43:05,207 --> 00:43:08,002
Is there something going on
that's making you glow like this?

383
00:43:10,337 --> 00:43:12,297
I would tell you, of course.

384
00:43:12,298 --> 00:43:14,675
Good, because I don't like secrets.

385
00:43:17,511 --> 00:43:18,846
Such a good girl.

386
00:43:21,307 --> 00:43:22,141
Turns me on.

387
00:43:35,321 --> 00:43:37,197
Which one do you want
for your company dinner?

388
00:43:38,449 --> 00:43:42,369
<i>He tends to drink more than usual
at his monthly branch dinners.</i>

389
00:43:43,704 --> 00:43:45,456
<i>And even more when he gets home.</i>

390
00:43:47,207 --> 00:43:49,001
<i>Then he passes out for the night.</i>

391
00:43:49,501 --> 00:43:52,921
You fly out on Friday.
We booked all your tickets.

392
00:43:55,966 --> 00:43:57,301
I thought I'd have longer.

393
00:43:57,885 --> 00:43:59,677
Sorry if this is catching you
on short notice,

394
00:43:59,678 --> 00:44:01,221
but I figured you could move fast.

395
00:44:04,600 --> 00:44:06,185
You figured that right.

396
00:44:07,936 --> 00:44:09,062
I don't have much.

397
00:44:09,063 --> 00:44:11,814
I'll give you the flight details
when we have everything worked out.

398
00:44:11,815 --> 00:44:13,025
"We"?

399
00:44:15,194 --> 00:44:17,404
You know, me and the other guy.

400
00:44:18,656 --> 00:44:19,573
Oh.

401
00:44:20,282 --> 00:44:21,116
Right.

402
00:44:26,372 --> 00:44:28,082
Your first half of the payment.

403
00:44:32,127 --> 00:44:34,253
Your son must have really missed his dad.

404
00:44:34,254 --> 00:44:35,505
There's a bit extra in there

405
00:44:35,506 --> 00:44:38,007
for you to take care of
your wife and son's travel expenses

406
00:44:38,008 --> 00:44:39,468
to meet you at the airport.

407
00:45:06,370 --> 00:45:07,370
Here.

408
00:45:07,371 --> 00:45:08,621
Oh, thanks, Kang.

409
00:45:10,416 --> 00:45:11,583
MS. JO EUN-SU

410
00:45:20,175 --> 00:45:22,719
Have you noticed
his new haircut and fancy clothes?

411
00:45:22,720 --> 00:45:24,138
I think he has a girlfriend.

412
00:45:24,763 --> 00:45:26,515
He says he's heading back to China.

413
00:45:29,059 --> 00:45:29,893
Who?

414
00:45:30,394 --> 00:45:31,687
Jang Kang, sir.

415
00:45:32,312 --> 00:45:34,189
I guess he saved enough to get home.

416
00:45:39,611 --> 00:45:41,738
<i>Get yourself ready
as quietly as possible,</i>

417
00:45:41,739 --> 00:45:43,030
<i>and watch out for Mr. Jin.</i>

418
00:45:43,031 --> 00:45:44,615
Not much gets by that guy.

419
00:45:44,616 --> 00:45:46,326
Be careful not to let on.

420
00:45:48,871 --> 00:45:49,747
Yeah.

421
00:46:30,496 --> 00:46:31,746
The gym's closed for the day,

422
00:46:31,747 --> 00:46:34,248
and you only suspended me
from attending classes.

423
00:46:34,249 --> 00:46:35,626
Isn't that right, sir?

424
00:46:51,266 --> 00:46:53,726
You've never gotten past white belt
all these years.

425
00:46:53,727 --> 00:46:55,229
Do you ever wonder why that is?

426
00:46:57,648 --> 00:46:59,816
From the moment you entered the gym,

427
00:46:59,817 --> 00:47:02,528
it was obvious that your reason
for being here...

428
00:47:04,696 --> 00:47:06,406
...stemmed from desperation.

429
00:47:08,951 --> 00:47:12,204
I gave you the worst-smelling partners,
and you didn't back off.

430
00:47:12,704 --> 00:47:15,248
I denied you opportunities to advance,
and you refused to quit.

431
00:47:15,249 --> 00:47:18,043
I just wanted to try to improve.

432
00:48:08,385 --> 00:48:10,261
JO EUN-SU

433
00:49:35,013 --> 00:49:36,348
Are you serious?

434
00:50:02,207 --> 00:50:03,208
Jo Eun-su.

435
00:50:06,044 --> 00:50:07,587
This was your last day here.

436
00:50:13,885 --> 00:50:15,262
Take care of yourself.

437
00:51:06,229 --> 00:51:09,399
Can I go with Eun-su
and visit my mother a little later?

438
00:51:09,900 --> 00:51:10,776
What for?

439
00:51:11,276 --> 00:51:13,653
She wants to bring her flowers
and say hello.

440
00:51:15,989 --> 00:51:16,865
You can go.

441
00:51:19,367 --> 00:51:20,951
And I'll be here when you get home.

442
00:51:20,952 --> 00:51:23,288
I know that.

443
00:51:41,807 --> 00:51:44,643
Tomorrow,
we'll have to do this without GPS.

444
00:51:47,187 --> 00:51:48,105
Hmm.

445
00:52:17,759 --> 00:52:19,136
{\an8}MINE

446
00:52:29,312 --> 00:52:31,815
- Hello, Mr. Noh.
- Hello, ma'am.

447
00:52:32,315 --> 00:52:33,899
- How are you?
- Fine. How are you?

448
00:52:33,900 --> 00:52:37,111
Yes, thanks. Did we have an appointment?
I don't seem to have you on my schedule.

449
00:52:37,112 --> 00:52:40,030
- No, we were just in the neighborhood.
- What a nice surprise. Have a seat.

450
00:52:40,031 --> 00:52:41,658
Good to see you.

451
00:53:10,312 --> 00:53:11,730
We're almost there.

452
00:53:13,982 --> 00:53:15,275
We're almost there.

453
00:53:16,359 --> 00:53:18,152
<i>Who else thinks
our deputy branch manager</i>

454
00:53:18,153 --> 00:53:21,071
should say a few words
to celebrate closing such a big deal, huh?

455
00:53:21,072 --> 00:53:23,490
- No speeches, please.
- Noh Jin-pyo.

456
00:53:23,491 --> 00:53:24,617
Noh Jin-pyo!

457
00:53:24,618 --> 00:53:27,369
I just did my job.
I appreciate it, but I can't.

458
00:53:27,370 --> 00:53:29,496
- Noh Jin-pyo! Noh Jin-pyo!
- Come on.

459
00:53:29,497 --> 00:53:34,293
Noh Jin-pyo!
Noh Jin-pyo! Noh Jin-pyo!

460
00:53:37,130 --> 00:53:38,547
- Yeah!
- Speech!

461
00:53:40,217 --> 00:53:41,843
I'm sure some of you

462
00:53:42,969 --> 00:53:45,054
would have loved to see me crash and burn,

463
00:53:45,055 --> 00:53:47,431
even though your bonuses
all depend on this deal.

464
00:53:48,516 --> 00:53:51,393
For those of you who thought a nice
corner office might become available,

465
00:53:51,394 --> 00:53:52,646
rest assured

466
00:53:53,605 --> 00:53:55,065
that Noh Jin-pyo

467
00:53:56,066 --> 00:53:57,399
is here to stay.

468
00:53:57,400 --> 00:53:58,526
For good.

469
00:53:59,527 --> 00:54:01,112
I fought for all of you.

470
00:54:02,197 --> 00:54:03,782
For the future of Golden One!

471
00:54:04,532 --> 00:54:05,824
- To us!
- Yeah!

472
00:54:19,589 --> 00:54:24,636
{\an8}SAN 1, DAECHI-RI, HYEONBUK-MYEON,
YANGYANG-GUN, GANGWON-DO

473
00:54:31,810 --> 00:54:33,436
Where the hell did you go?

474
00:54:36,064 --> 00:54:37,983
That's no nursing home.

475
00:54:46,199 --> 00:54:50,912
MR. NOH JIN-PYO,
YOU HAVEN'T BOOKED ACCOMMODATIONS

476
00:54:57,502 --> 00:54:59,712
{\an8}YOUR TRIP IS COMING UP, MR. NOH JIN-PYO!

477
00:54:59,713 --> 00:55:02,841
{\an8}HURRY BEFORE YOUR SHANGHAI HOTEL
DISCOUNT EXPIRES!

